# Echo campaign B, "new setup": the same TCP echo servers (C, Java, Erlang; benchmarks/echo/) with BEAM
# busy-waiting on and off, with tests chosen for the energy meter: every load lasts long enough for many samples,
# and two tests keep connections open, where busy-waiting matters most. Every server as built and Erlang also as
# -nobw (C and Java skipped), each in Docker and natively, in one shuffled order. Message: "Hello, Servers!" (15 B).
# 5 tests x 4 servers x 2 deployments x 5 repeats = 200 measurements, about 5 h.
#   make run CONFIG=campaigns/paper/echo-new.config
# Decisions (2026-10-16, after the supervisor meeting):
#   - connect sleep (one message per connection, 0.1 s apart) with 100 and 1000 clients: 10 s and 100 s of load
#   - nosleep with 10,000 clients at once (the most this laptop handles; 20,000 fails for all three servers),
#     5 rounds one after the other, ~15 s of load instead of ~3 s
#   - burst: 100 clients, 2000 messages each back to back on one connection (the server is always busy)
#   - stream: 100 clients, 10 messages per second each for 30 s (the server waits between messages)
#   - same machine settings as the busy-wait campaign: CPU fixed at 1800 MHz, 5 repeats, no idle measurement
MACHINE=minimal
ENV_CPU_SPEED=1800
MEASURE=echo
VARIANTS=nobw:ERL_FLAGS=+sbwt none +sbwtdcpu none +sbwtdio none
DEPLOY=container native
REPEATS=5
IDLE_SECONDS=0
ECHO_CONNECT_CLIENTS=100 1000
ECHO_CONNECT_SPACING_SECONDS=0.1
ECHO_NOSLEEP_CLIENTS=10000
ECHO_NOSLEEP_ROUNDS=5
ECHO_BURST_CLIENTS=100
ECHO_BURST_MESSAGES=2000
ECHO_STREAM_CLIENTS=100
ECHO_STREAM_RATE_PER_SECOND=10
ECHO_STREAM_DURATION_SECONDS=30
ECHO_SIZES_BYTES=15
